{"school":{"dbn":"06M103","name":"Dos Puentes Elementary School","boro":"Manhattan","district":"06","district_label":"District 6","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EC|EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"K-5","status":"open","enrollment":420,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"185 WADSWORTH AVENUE, MANHATTAN, NY 10033","phone":"212-781-1803","website":"DOSPUENTES.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/68262","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"Dos Puentes Elementary is a full Dual Language School that works to support all children developing bilingualism and bilteracy in English and Spanish. Families are our partners supported through monthly Family Fridays, Evening and Weekend school events such as potlucks, fitness night, concerts, fall festival, and talent show and family workshops.  Education is rigorous, inclusive, and supports children's academic and social emotional development. Dos Puentes also promotes the arts through a full music and dance program, and partnership with Studio in a School. Additionally we have a rigorous hands on science and wellness program with PE , Wellness in the School and a school garden. We have a partnership with Teachers College Columbia University and City College of New York to support future teachers, and ongoing research in the field of bilingual education. \nPlease join one of our school tours by calling (212) 781-1803. This school has a Bilingual Special Education (BSE) program: Open to students recommended for Bilingual Special Education (BSE) on their Individualized Education Plan (IEP). If your child is recommended for BSE on their IEP and you have questions, visit www.schools.nyc.gov/specializedprograms or contact BSEprograms@schools.nyc.gov.","start_time":"8:20 AM","end_time":"2:40 PM","languages":"Spanish","subway":"1 to 181st St; A to 175th St","bus":"Bx11, Bx13, Bx3, Bx35, Bx36, Bx7, M100, M101, M3, M4, M5, M98","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":null,"latitude":4